{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Adjacent measured evidence from the lock-hold instrumentation on [rebar:7084-4e33-e698-42dd] (2026-08-07). Not a new root cause for this ticket, but it bears on how often the undeliverable-warning path is entered.\n\nThe tickets-branch push has a SECOND way to go pending that is not a rejected push at all: `push.py`'s merge leg acquires the store write lock with a **15s** budget (`_PUSH_MERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT`, `attempts=1`) and, on LockTimeout at `push.py:355`, gives up and leaves the push PENDING with only a WARNING — the `tickets branch push-retry merge skipped: write lock busy; push stays pending` line already recorded on 7084.\n\nMeasured: a single `compact-on-close` holds that same lock for **48.1s** on a 7-event ticket and for **over 20 minutes** on a 75-event one (99% of it a per-event `git log --full-history` walk inside the critical section; see 7084 for the profile). A 15s budget cannot survive that. So under ordinary parallel-agent load the push-pending state is reached routinely by lock contention, not only by a declining remote — and on the async / library / MCP paths this ticket covers, that WARNING is discarded exactly the same way. The two defects compound: contention makes push-pending common, and this ticket makes it invisible.\n\nNothing implemented; the compaction remediation is proposed and awaiting operator approval on 7084."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786115976258047001,"uuid":"17262f35-eeca-45ea-b89d-b2a680bb563b"}